# Copy to client/.env when you want to (a) connect the Supabase database (bottom of this file)
# or (b) host the site WITHOUT the Node server.
# If this file is absent: demo mode, and the forms post to our own server at /api/... (the default).

# Once the Supabase lines at the bottom are filled in, the forms save straight to the
# database and show up in the Admin dashboard. Nothing else is needed for free hosting.
# Options A / B below are only if you ALSO want each form emailed to you.

# --- Option A: a free form service (works on any static host) ---------------
# Sign up at https://web3forms.com (free, no account needed beyond your email),
# paste the access key it emails you, and uncomment these three lines.
# VITE_FORM_MODE=endpoint
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://api.web3forms.com/submit
# VITE_FORM_ACCESS_KEY=paste-your-web3forms-key-here

# Formspree works the same way (no access key needed):
# VITE_FORM_MODE=endpoint
# VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://formspree.io/f/yourFormId

# --- Option B: Netlify Forms (only if you host on Netlify) -----------------
# Nothing else to set up — submissions appear in the Netlify dashboard.
# VITE_FORM_MODE=netlify

# --- Database + admin login (Supabase) -------------------------------------
# Leave these empty and the site runs in DEMO MODE: sample data, saved only in
# your browser, with six demo log-ins (password demo1234) on the /login page.
# Fill them in (see SUPABASE_SETUP.md) to use the real shared database.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste-the-anon-public-key-here
